{"title":"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 2","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/0/8b044ad1ab87ac3a26893a320b3dce8696c891c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbb{R}^{+}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"26\" height=\"17\" /> be the set of positive real numbers. Find all functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/c/14cfa0e74c45365955c72ca408212ad8b3a0fe21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f:\\mathbb{R}^{+}\\rightarrow\\mathbb{R}^{+}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" /> such that, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/7481f9e7721a48e9a54a11c23d491d953096f4eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y \\in \\mathbb{R}^{+}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" />,<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/2/c623d226331401de700d000f6c1cc868f268b65f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(xy + f(x)) = xf(y) + 2\\]\" width=\"202\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Make the following substitutions to the equation:\n</p><p>1. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/7/4b7c088bb6d073e955436c3e7834fc84741ca4d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, 1) \\rightarrow f(x + f(x)) = xf(1) + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"265\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>2. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/9/af9987276fa5e68e2eb164515df47da24d0ce245.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1, x + f(x)) \\rightarrow f(x + f(x) + f(1)) = f(x + f(x)) + 2 = xf(1) + 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"527\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>3. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/c/24c635be2208239c3845048a4a26b905342ad228.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x, 1 + \\frac{f(1)}{x}) \\rightarrow f(x + f(x) + f(1)) = xf\\biggl(1 + \\frac{f(1)}{x}\\biggr) + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"454\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>It then follows from (2) and (3) that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/9/f99b973500d274adb9952791f759ad9d63411770.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1 + \\frac{f(1)}{x}) = f(1) + \\frac{2}{x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"191\" height=\"40\" />, so we know that this function is linear for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/3767f0665ea4d5f0e9c58452fc5782b42a8a65a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />. Substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/f/12fa44614c0c514290222b7ab5317272df05c948.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = ax+b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" /> and solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> in the functional equation; we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/1/1a1dbc7eb740a460e9c072504ce0b1849307feb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x + 1 \\forall x &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"157\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Now, we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/3767f0665ea4d5f0e9c58452fc5782b42a8a65a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0d31941fa44c031f0164b5b06fd6c7883759683.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\le 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/2593a5aac2ac3f0bce25639dacaf8db416fd2daa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/b/ccb7aaa812712226fa2e678b3e74ba45e31bc820.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy + f(x) &gt; x &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"147\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af632c015831a66f310bee7b73f362712a1a621.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(xy + f(x)) = xy + x + 2 = xf(y) + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"313\" height=\"20\" />. It becomes clear then that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055373944920cd953bf7c41993883e5b07568b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(y) = y + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" /> as well, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/2593a5aac2ac3f0bce25639dacaf8db416fd2daa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"20\" /> is the only solution to the functional equation.\n</p><p>~jkmmm3\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO\" title=\"2023 USAMO\">2023 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2023\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2023 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"htt